@base = http://localhost:5125
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### Transaction Script: withdraw 100 € (one script does everything)
POST {{base}}/scripts/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100 }

### Active Record: read Alice (same database: the withdrawal above is there)
GET {{base}}/records/accounts/{{alice}}

### Active Record: transfer from Alice to Bob (the route coordinates, the objects check and save)
POST {{base}}/records/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 250 }

### Transaction Script: read Bob, with his latest operations
GET {{base}}/scripts/accounts/{{bob}}

### Transaction Script: transfer to an unknown account (404, and Alice's debit is rolled back)
POST {{base}}/scripts/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "amount": 50 }

### Same rule in both styles: insufficient balance (400)
POST {{base}}/records/accounts/{{bob}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 99999 }

### Open an account (201)
POST {{base}}/scripts/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "owner": "Chloe", "initialDeposit": 50 }
